% The Ponens policies apply-formal-methods, as a program of Logical English for LPS.
%
% Written by lpsPlus's ponens_twin.pl (docs/migration/ponens.md) from 8
% Ponens policies, whose files are in sources/ (Ponens: github.com/imandra-ai/
% ponens, MIT licence), with 8 Ponens traces as its scenarios.
%
% Each step of a trace is an action of the session Ponens recorded. Each
% policy is a causal law that records a breach: at the step where the policy
% fails, when the step ends, or at the end of the session when the policy
% looks forward. Where a scenario has a comment above it, the comment is what
% Ponens's own evaluator (`ponens trace check --json`) says of the same
% policies on that trace.
%
% DISCLAIMER. This program was written by a translator from the policies of
% another system. It is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind,
% express or implied, including any warranty that it is accurate, complete or
% fit for a particular purpose. The translation may be wrong: check it against
% its source before relying on it. It is not legal, regulatory or other
% professional advice. Its authors accept no liability for any loss or damage
% arising from its use.

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 50.

the events are:
    step *a step* is a *a kind*; known as step_is_a.
    step *a step* shows *a sign*; known as step_shows.
    step *a step* comes after step *an other step* in its chain; known as chain_link.
    step *a step* comes after step *an other step* on its target; known as target_link.
    step *a step* ends; known as step_ends.
    the trace shows *a sign*; known as trace_shows.
    item *an item* of *a collection* has *a value* as *a field*; known as item_field.
    artifact *an artifact* is made by step *a step*; known as made_by_event.
    step *a step* uses artifact *an artifact*; known as uses_event.
    artifact *an artifact* is a *a kind* artifact; known as artifact_kind_event.
    artifact *an artifact* derives from artifact *an other artifact*; known as derives_event.
    artifact *an artifact* is a verification goal for artifact *an other artifact*; known as goal_target_event.
    file *a file* is edited; known as edited_event.
    file *a file* is declared as modified; known as declared_event.
    the session ends; known as session_ends.

the fluents are:
    step *a step* was a *a kind*; known as was_a.
    step *a step* has shown *a sign*; known as has_shown.
    step *a step* is in the chain of step *an other step*; known as in_chain.
    step *a step* shares a target with step *an other step*; known as shares_target.
    step *a step* has ended; known as has_ended.
    the trace has shown *a sign*; known as trace_has_shown.
    item *an item* of *a collection* had *a value* as *a field*; known as item_had.
    artifact *an artifact* was made by step *a step*; known as made_by.
    step *a step* used artifact *an artifact*; known as used.
    artifact *an artifact* was a *a kind* artifact; known as artifact_kind.
    artifact *an artifact* derived from artifact *an other artifact*; known as derived.
    artifact *an artifact* was a verification goal for artifact *an other artifact*; known as goal_target.
    file *a file* was edited; known as edited.
    file *a file* was declared as modified; known as declared.
    step *a step* meets *a condition*; known as meets.
    the trace meets *a condition*; known as trace_meets.
    artifact *an artifact* meets *a condition*; known as artifact_meets.
    artifact *an artifact* meets *a condition* with artifact *an other artifact*; known as artifact_meets_with.
    the policy *a policy* is broken at step *a step*; known as broken_at.
    the policy *a policy* is broken; known as broken.

the knowledge base apply formal methods includes:

% What a trace records, kept to the end of the session.
when step a step is a a kind
then step the step was a the kind.

when step a step shows a sign
then step the step has shown the sign.

when step a step comes after step an other step in its chain
then step the other step is in the chain of step the step.

when step a step comes after step an other step on its target
then step the other step shares a target with step the step.

when step a step ends
then step the step has ended.

when the trace shows a sign
then the trace has shown the sign.

when item an item of a collection has a value as a field
then item the item of the collection had the value as the field.

when artifact an artifact is made by step a step
then artifact the artifact was made by step the step.

when step a step uses artifact an artifact
then step the step used artifact the artifact.

when artifact an artifact is a a kind artifact
then artifact the artifact was a the kind artifact.

when artifact an artifact derives from artifact an other artifact
then artifact the artifact derived from artifact the other artifact.

when artifact an artifact is a verification goal for artifact an other artifact
then artifact the artifact was a verification goal for artifact the other artifact.

when file a file is edited
then file the file was edited.

when file a file is declared as modified
then file the file was declared as modified.


% counterexample_triggers_fix (warning): G(Verify ∧ refuted → F(EditFile))
% Finding a bug via formal verification is only useful if the bug gets fixed. A refutation should lead to a code change.
step a step meets "it or a later step is a EditFile" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step >= the step
    and step the second step was a EditFile at the time.

when the session ends
    and step a step has ended
    and step the step was a Verify
    and step the step has shown "refuted"
    and it is not the case that step the step meets "it or a later step is a EditFile"
then the policy counterexample_triggers_fix is broken at step the step.

% decomposition_drives_tests (warning): (G(Decompose → F(GenerateTests))) ∧ G(Decompose → (produced_by(codelogician) ∨ oracle_type(codelogician)))
% Region decomposition maps a function's disjoint behavioral cases; its payoff is a high-coverage test per region. A decomposition with no tests generated from it leaves that value on the table.
step a step meets "if it is a Decompose then it it or a later step is a GenerateTests" at a time if
    it is not the case that step the step was a Decompose at the time.

step a step meets "it or a later step is a GenerateTests" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step >= the step
    and step the second step was a GenerateTests at the time.

step a step meets "if it is a Decompose then it it or a later step is a GenerateTests" at a time if
    step the step meets "it or a later step is a GenerateTests" at the time.

step a step meets "not (if it is a Decompose then it it or a later step is a GenerateTests)" at a time if
    it is not the case that step the step meets "if it is a Decompose then it it or a later step is a GenerateTests" at the time.

the trace meets "some step: not (if it is a Decompose then it it or a later step is a GenerateTests)" at a time if
    step a step has ended at the time
    and step the step meets "not (if it is a Decompose then it it or a later step is a GenerateTests)" at the time.

the trace meets "every step if it is a Decompose then it it or a later step is a GenerateTests" at a time if
    it is not the case that the trace meets "some step: not (if it is a Decompose then it it or a later step is a GenerateTests)" at the time.

step a step meets "if it is a Decompose then it shows produced_by(codelogician) or shows oracle_type(codelogician)" at a time if
    it is not the case that step the step was a Decompose at the time.

step a step meets "shows produced_by(codelogician) or shows oracle_type(codelogician)" at a time if
    step the step has shown "produced_by(codelogician)" at the time.

step a step meets "shows produced_by(codelogician) or shows oracle_type(codelogician)" at a time if
    step the step has shown "oracle_type(codelogician)" at the time.

step a step meets "if it is a Decompose then it shows produced_by(codelogician) or shows oracle_type(codelogician)" at a time if
    step the step meets "shows produced_by(codelogician) or shows oracle_type(codelogician)" at the time.

step a step meets "not (if it is a Decompose then it shows produced_by(codelogician) or shows oracle_type(codelogician))" at a time if
    it is not the case that step the step meets "if it is a Decompose then it shows produced_by(codelogician) or shows oracle_type(codelogician)" at the time.

the trace meets "some step: not (if it is a Decompose then it shows produced_by(codelogician) or shows oracle_type(codelogician))" at a time if
    step a step has ended at the time
    and step the step meets "not (if it is a Decompose then it shows produced_by(codelogician) or shows oracle_type(codelogician))" at the time.

the trace meets "every step if it is a Decompose then it shows produced_by(codelogician) or shows oracle_type(codelogician)" at a time if
    it is not the case that the trace meets "some step: not (if it is a Decompose then it shows produced_by(codelogician) or shows oracle_type(codelogician))" at the time.

the trace meets "the trace: it and every later step if it is a Decompose then it it or a later step is a GenerateTests and it and every later step if it is a Decompose then it shows produced_by(codelogician) or shows oracle_type(codelogician)" at a time if
    the trace meets "every step if it is a Decompose then it it or a later step is a GenerateTests" at the time
    and the trace meets "every step if it is a Decompose then it shows produced_by(codelogician) or shows oracle_type(codelogician)" at the time.

when the session ends
    and it is not the case that the trace meets "the trace: it and every later step if it is a Decompose then it it or a later step is a GenerateTests and it and every later step if it is a Decompose then it shows produced_by(codelogician) or shows oracle_type(codelogician)"
then the policy decomposition_drives_tests is broken.

% formalization_is_analyzed (warning): (G(Formalize → F(Verify ∨ StateSpaceAnalysis))) ∧ G(Verify → (produced_by(codelogician) ∨ oracle_type(codelogician))) ∧ G(StateSpaceAnalysis → (produced_by(codelogician) ∨ oracle_type(codelogician)))
% A formalization that is never verified or decomposed is dead weight — building a model only pays off when the model is actually reasoned over, so an unused Formalize is a flagged gap.
step a step meets "if it is a Formalize then it it or a later step is a Verify or is a StateSpaceAnalysis" at a time if
    it is not the case that step the step was a Formalize at the time.

step a step meets "is a Verify or is a StateSpaceAnalysis" at a time if
    step the step was a Verify at the time.

step a step meets "is a Verify or is a StateSpaceAnalysis" at a time if
    step the step was a StateSpaceAnalysis at the time.

step a step meets "it or a later step is a Verify or is a StateSpaceAnalysis" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
    and the second step >= the step
    and step the second step meets "is a Verify or is a StateSpaceAnalysis" at the time.

step a step meets "if it is a Formalize then it it or a later step is a Verify or is a StateSpaceAnalysis" at a time if
    step the step meets "it or a later step is a Verify or is a StateSpaceAnalysis" at the time.

