% verified_claims_are_fidelity_checked (warning): ((F SourceCode) → G(Verify → F(ConformanceResult(passed)))) ∧ G(Verify → (produced_by(codelogician) ∨ oracle_type(codelogician))) ∧ G(ConformanceResult → (produced_by(codelogician) ∨ oracle_type(codelogician)))
% A proof holds of the MODEL. When the model was translated from real code, a fidelity (conformance) check is what links the two — without it a 'verified' verdict is only provisional and may not reflect the deployed system. The requirement is guarded by `F SourceCode` so it applies only when there IS source to conform to: a spec-first / authored-IML session (no SourceCode artifact) passes vacuously, since the IML itself is the artifact, not a translation. Fidelity is optional in the current flow, so a missing check on code-derived models is a flagged gap, not a hard failure (hence warning).
the trace meets "some step is a SourceCode" at a time if
    step a step has ended at the time
    and step the step was a SourceCode at the time.

the trace meets "the trace: if it it or a later step is a SourceCode then it it and every later step if it is a Verify then it it or a later step shows ConformanceResult(passed)" at a time if
    it is not the case that the trace meets "some step is a SourceCode" at the time.

step a step meets "if it is a Verify then it it or a later step shows ConformanceResult(passed)" at a time if
    it is not the case that step the step was a Verify at the time.

step a step meets "it or a later step shows ConformanceResult(passed)" at a time if
    step a second step has ended at the time
